A||N||8||Ambush||Cheapest V-8 Swap Kit||||1||
Z||000000||Ambush||10-27-2001||06:16 PM||||OK people, this subject has been BEAT to death, Yet I never got a good answer. I want a V-8!!!!!! I am as cheap as they come. I can get engine fairly cheap so I don't need any help with that. What I do need help with is the kits that go into doing a swap. What all do I need. Can I just go and get a caddy engine and stuff it in? or is it a little more complicated than that? Is  there a V-8 that doesn't need a kit to fit in? If not which is the cheapest?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Juiced_V8||10-27-2001||06:48 PM||||to go cheapest you would still need to get archies basic kit its a good kit i bought my fiero with the archie delux kit installed and the trans was bad i am still putting it back together after taking it all apart and painting\detailing the engine\kit archies kit is a good deal honestly and the parts fit like there supposed to i basically re installed the whole kit with a beefed tranny and it all went back together super easy<P>------------------<BR>86 gt v8 fogger set up sold going to get a simple sniper system with a plate||||reg||12
Z||000002||Bazooka||10-27-2001||07:00 PM||||*********************************<BR>Ambush,    You might consider a Caddy 4.5 with Throttle Body Injection. They are readily available, and you can use the matched Caddy trans or the 125c with little modification. For info on this conversion, see Rockcrawls webpage at <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/</A>  <BR> <BR>**********************************<BR>   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ambush:<BR><B>OK people, this subject has been BEAT to death, Yet I never got a good answer. I want a V-8!!!!!! I am as cheap as they come. I can get engine fairly cheap so I don't need any help with that. What I do need help with is the kits that go into doing a swap. What all do I need. Can I just go and get a caddy engine and stuff it in? or is it a little more complicated than that? Is  there a V-8 that doesn't need a kit to fit in? If not which is the cheapest?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*********************************<p>[This message has been edited by Bazooka (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektrum-87GT||10-27-2001||10:50 PM||||i really dont think a cheap v8 swap is possible, i've been looking into it for over a year and it seems like 4k is the cheapest you can make it and still turn out with a decent swap. just break it down<BR>2k for a decent crate engine<BR>2k for all the swap parts necessary(including the kit)<P>4k is also on the way low end.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ambush||10-28-2001||12:06 AM||||I was check'n out Archies V-8 Economy kit at 950.00 I can do that, but that would be as much as I want to spend on the kit. Do I need the other things that are in theDelux kit? or is there a way around it?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-28-2001||12:07 AM||||4k is about the low end for a small block. from what i've been reading depending on what you find and what work you can do yourself a pre northstar caddy swap can be as much as 1/4 of that cost. rockcrawl or bubbajoe could give firmer numbers on it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ambush||10-28-2001||09:36 PM||||Does anyone have those firmer numbers?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||10-29-2001||12:06 AM||||Well, you're gonna need  pretty much everything in Archie's Master Build kit.  If you can scrounge or source some of those parts cheap, great.  Get the econo kit and add the rest of the stuff yourself.  But start with the Master Build kit as your inventory and start pricing the parts yourself.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rgeeinc||10-29-2001||02:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ambush:<BR><B>Does anyone have those firmer numbers?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ambush, just remember you get what you pay for. If you want some real numbers, Price Archies Master build Kit, don't forget you have to buy a motor, If you buy a used one and you don't know the history, you will have to rebuild that. No sense putting something in a car you don't know about. It will just cost you time and money latter. Or you could buy a crate engine. (Prices are published everywhere). $2500.00 is a good round number, for a middle of the road carte motor. LM1 comes to mind. So now you have a kit and a motor, approximate price $5500.00.<BR>All you have to do now is add 10% for miscellaneous items, and you will be pretty close.<BR>That price is if you are doing all the work your self.  You can always adjust the numbers as you see fit. Price of the engine exc. But the kit will be the same and the extras may very a little, (not much). if you buy anything but the Master Build Kit.<P>The 10% is for the things you will run into that you didn't count on. They always seem to pop up.     If you get away with a finished car for less then $6000.00 you will be doing good. For that price you should have something to be proud of and will last you for some time, and will be a dependable ride.<BR>That's my opinion and I am just trying to be real<BR>    <BR>Hope you get what you want.  GOOD LUCK.<P>||||reg||1
